Your categories add to $11,661 against an $11,900 statement, so $239 is still unaccounted for. Don't send it like this with the gap silent — either find the missing charges or add a line: 'Unmatched charges, $239, see missing-receipt log.' Also note that the $2,350 equipment line will likely get different treatment from the ingredients line; keep it as its own category (as you have) and let your accountant rule on it rather than folding it into supplies.

```json
{
  "w9_chase_list": {
    "as_of": "November",
    "outstanding": [
      {"payee": "Highest total first", "paid_ytd": 6200, "requests_sent": 2, "next_step": "Phone call this week, not a third email"},
      {"payee": "Second", "paid_ytd": 3100, "requests_sent": 1, "next_step": "Email with the blank form attached and a deadline"},
      {"payee": "Third", "paid_ytd": 1450, "requests_sent": 1, "next_step": "Ask at next scheduled job, in person"},
      {"payee": "Fourth", "paid_ytd": 700, "requests_sent": 0, "next_step": "First request now, with the year-end explanation"}
    ],
    "on_file": 5,
    "chase_rules": [
      "Sort by amount paid, not by how easy they are to reach - the biggest undocumented total is the biggest exposure",
      "Every request in writing, dated, and kept - the request log itself is a record your accountant will want",
      "Attach the blank form every time; friction, not refusal, is the usual cause",
      "Set an internal deadline two weeks before your accountant's filing deadline, not on it"
    ]
  }
}
```

Replace the placeholders with your real names and totals, and keep the request log with dates. If someone still hasn't responded by your deadline, that fact — with the log showing your attempts — goes to your accountant, who will tell you how they want it handled. Don't hold the whole filing hostage to the last form.

```json
{
  "contractor_summary_2026": {
    "payees": [
      {"payee": "Bookkeeper", "total": 3600, "w9": "on file"},
      {"payee": "Web designer", "total": 2750, "w9": "on file"},
      {"payee": "Cleaner", "total": 1800, "w9": "missing - requested twice"},
      {"payee": "Snow removal", "total": 1150, "w9": "missing - requested once"},
      {"payee": "Sign painter", "total": 640, "w9": "missing - not yet requested"}
    ],
    "grand_total": 9940,
